I was hanging out with the cool kids in rec.games.roguelike.nethack when 
Arthur J. O'Dwyer got out a spraycan and scrawled the following:
>  On Mon, 11 Dec 2006, Simon Richard Clarkstone wrote:
> > Arthur J. O'Dwyer wrote:
> >> http://www.contrib.andrew.cmu.edu/~ajo/free-software/nethack/wish343.diff
> >> 
> >> I just "finished" a patch to the wishing code that lets the player wish
> >> for --- and get --- objects already existing in monsters' inventories,
> [...]
>     Do you think it would really unbalance the game to let the player
>  recover the Quest item by using up one wish? I think of wishes as
>  insanely valuable, but then I have next to no experience with the late
>  game.

It is necessary to kill the Quest nemesis in order to get the Bell and
complete the game, so being able to wish your Quest artifact out of the
nemesis' hands, or off the floor at their feet, could be very
unbalancing if the change of ownership of the artifact makes the nemesis
much easier to beat.  Examples are

The Tsurugi (risk of bisection)
The Staff (risk of draining)
...and anything that has a good defensive capability when carried (eyes,
orbs)

You might consider it balanced by the way that the nemesis can steal the
artifact back if you keep it in your inventory while attacking them.

